    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Footnote for Schedule XVIII</span>
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:48.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:48.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Non-Associate Company</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Description</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Balch and Bingham</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Monthly electric bills paid by Southern Company Services (SCS) on behalf of our tenant, Balch &amp; Bingham.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Department of Energy (DOE)</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Research and development grants/cooperative agreements where SCS acts as either prime or sub-recipient of federal financial assistance funding from DOE. SCS collaborates with the Federal Government/DOE receiving and contributing funding for research agreements involving cutting edge energy technologies that further a public purpose aligning with DOE&#8217;s research and programs.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Electric Power Research Institute</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Analysis of Battery Storage and Distributed Resources to Support Fleet Charging Infrastructure, Batter Energy Storage Thermal Management and Systems Performance, Beneficial Use of Fly Ash in a Road Base Fill: Environmental Monitoring, Digital Demonstration Facility (DDF) Installation and Support, Engineering and Project Management Services for Renewable &amp; Natural Gas Fuel Cell Demonstration Project, Liquid Organic Hydrogen Carrier Demo, SPC M&amp;D Center EPRI Combustion Dynamics Algorithm Project Estimate, and Support for Water Research and Conservation Center Design and Construction.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Exxon Mobil Technology &amp; Engineering Company</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Reimbursable agreement with SCS and ExxonMobil for testing carbon capture technologies at the National Carbon Capture Center in Wilsonville, AL. Costs are fully reimbursable by SCS due to testing being privately funded by ExxonMobil and activities being outside of the NCCC/Department of Energy (DOE) government agreement scope. ExxonMobil is reimbursing SCS for design engineering, operation, materials, electricity and natural gas usage, and other costs associated with ExxonMobil's testing.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Georgia Nuclear Decommissioning</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Management and administration of the Georgia Power Company Nuclear Decommissioning Trusts (Qualified &amp; Non-Qualified).</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Georgia Power Charitable Foundation</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Management and administration of the Georgia Power Company Charitable Foundation Trust.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">KC8 Capture Technologies Ltd</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">KC8 Technologies collaborates with Southern Company Services (SCS) on certain research, development, testing, and/or evaluation activities at the National Carbon Capture Center (NCCC) related to the use, operation, testing, improvement, and/or optimization of SRI's technology. The NCCC provides the infrastructure in which third-party developers' technologies are installed and tested to generate data for performance verification under industrially realistic operating conditions. Costs are reimbursable by SCS due to being outside of the NCCC/Department of Energy (DOE) government agreement scope. Technology collaboration agreements outline contract limitations and scope of the additional work being requested to be done by SCS.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Southern System Master Retirement Trust</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Management and administration of the Southern Company System Master Retirement Trust (Pension).</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">SRI International</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">SRI International (SRI) collaborates with Southern Company Services (SCS) on certain research, development, testing, and/or evaluation activities at the National Carbon Capture Center (NCCC) related to the use, operation, testing, improvement, and/or optimization of SRI's technology. The NCCC provides the infrastructure in which third-party developers' technologies are installed and tested to generate data for performance verification under industrially realistic operating conditions. Costs are fully reimbursable by SCS due to being outside of the NCCC/Department of Energy (DOE) government agreement scope. Technology collaboration agreements outline contract limitations and scope of the additional work being requested to be done by SCS.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Transmission Studies</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Studies to determine impact of and availability to third party wholesale usage of transmission lines.</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
